Month 1 – learned networking fundamentals:
In the first month of my cybersecurity journey I learned many of the networking fundamentals required to understand how internet works , this included topics like :
DNS , SUBNETTING , OSI MODEL , TCP/IP MODEL , DHCP , ROUTING , NAT , PAT , IP ADDRESSING , ARP , LAN , VLAN , SWITCH and many more topics.

I also did some lab work with kali linux where I learned commands like traceroute , ip a , ip route , ifconfig , ping and some nmap commands.
When I learned the fundamentals of networking everything became way clearer to me and pretty easy to understand like seeing my own ip and the subnet mask etc.
